  "characters": [
    {
      "id": "rowan",
      "name": "Rowan Vale",
      "summary": "A ranger of the Ash Guard, raised between forge smoke and night watches. A scar crosses their left brow, and they are searching for a missing sibling in the pine forest.",
      "history": "Rowan grew up at the edge of Vado Gris, where the forge never quite went cold. They learned to read metal before letters and joined the Ash Guard at sixteen to pay off the family debt. For years they covered the east wall at night, listening for anything moving under the pines.\n\nThe night of the fire, Rowan's younger sibling Mira went to find a lost child and did not come back. Rowan found only a brass buckle and a trail of ash leading into the woods. Since then they train with a discipline that unsettles the other guards and save every coin for the next search.",
      "personality": "Direct, dry, and protective past the point of reason. Rowan distrusts anyone who has never been hungry, but cannot leave someone behind. They relax by carving wooden spoons and humming badly tuned tavern songs.",
      "relationships": "Mira Vale, younger sibling, missing. Captain Ordo owes Rowan two lives and is a little afraid of them. Tomas the armorer keeps a stool by the forge and a bowl of broth every winter.",
      "tags": [
        "fantasy",
        "ranger",
        "ash guard"
      ],
